; config fixedblk_banks.env
; config fixedblk_fixed.env
; config fixedblk_untold.env
; config fixedblk_host.env
; A region in fixed memory that the compiler is told of (`define FIXED_REGIONS 1`, which gives
; -ffwork: lathe/host/README.md, "Command lines"). In fixedblk_banks.env the region fwork is in
; bank 4 and libfixb in bank 3, so libfixb's functions with a block, and add8, which runs inside
; one with a pointer into the region, are kept in fixed memory. In fixedblk_fixed.env the region
; is in fixed memory and the compiler knows it: the blocks map nothing, no call in them is
; flagged, and the linker keeps nothing, so all of libfixb is in bank 3, add8 reading the region
; through its pointer from there. In fixedblk_untold.env the region is fixed but the compiler is
; not told: the blocks map nothing, and their functions are kept as in the banks. The output is
; the same in every configuration, and all in one (fixedblk_host.env). The compiler told and the
; region in a bank is link error 62 (lathe/tests/test_lk_unmapped.py).
module fixedblk

import libfco
import libfixb

pub func main()
  libfixb.fill(3)
  libfco.hex(libfixb.sum())
  libfco.put(' ')
  libfco.hex(libfixb.get(5))
  libfco.put(10)
end
